        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/walkingtarget/{size}/4833_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-26T18:47:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You're pretty much doing it. I think I'm fairly safe saying that the community tries to not gatekeep, so don't feel like a poseur.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/greaterthangames/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">GTG</a> and <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/handelabragames\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Handelabra</a> (the company behind the video game implementation) both have Twitch channels. There's also a fan-run Discord (called the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/RuJbCV\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Realm of Discord</a>, because of course it is) and a <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/sentinelsmultiverse/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">subreddit</a> if you use those platforms. <a href=\"https://patreon.com/theletterspage\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">The Letters Page Patreon</a> is another point-of-contact if you really feel like it (with the Contributor level getting access to another Discord). Finally, there's a fan-run, but officially recognized <a href=\"https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Main_Page\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">wiki</a> for everything Sentinel Comics. That's saying nothing of the various company/individual's Twitter accounts or things like the extensive entries on TV Tropes for <em>SotM</em> content.</p>\n<p>Hang out in enough of those places for long enough and you'll see a bunch of the same names cropping up, but participate to the level you want - you're welcome to hang out anywhere.</p>",
